Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: apollo: match front camera digital supply to stock

The merged device tree read from this Apollo's running LineageOS fixes
PM8150A LDO2 (L2C) at 1080000 uV. Its regulator sysfs telemetry confirms
min=max=actual=1080000 uV. The front sensor's cam_vdig entry is also
1080000 uV. This rail has no other consumers in the native Apollo DTS.
Use that board-proven nominal voltage instead of the 1.20-1.304 V range.

This corrects a verified board description mismatch. It is not by itself
proof that all intermittent front sensor probe failures are solved.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-xiaomi-apollo.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-xiaomi-apollo.dts
@@ -486,11 +486,11 @@
 			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
 		};
 
-		/* Toegevoegd uit vendor DTSI */
-		vreg_l2c_1p2: ldo2 {
-			regulator-name = "vreg_l2c_1p2";
-			regulator-min-microvolt = <1200000>;
-			regulator-max-microvolt = <1304000>;
+		/* S5K3T2 digital supply: fixed 1.08 V in Apollo's running Android DT. */
+		vreg_l2c_1p08: ldo2 {
+			regulator-name = "vreg_l2c_1p08";
+			regulator-min-microvolt = <1080000>;
+			regulator-max-microvolt = <1080000>;
 			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
 		};
 
@@ -1442,7 +1442,7 @@
 		reg = <0x10>;
 
 		avdd-supply = <&vreg_l3p>;
-		dvdd-supply = <&vreg_l2c_1p2>;
+		dvdd-supply = <&vreg_l2c_1p08>;
 		dovdd-supply = <&vreg_l1c_1p8>;
 
 		clocks = <&camcc CAM_CC_MCLK4_CLK>;
